expeditions/2026-06-20-aoyagi-full/synthesis.md:724:cover's `toric-ray-cert.md` (#142) — decorrelated adversarial Codex produced the exact combined-ray formula, cover hand-re-derived + SETTLED the decisive datum (MC-RLCT attempted as a guide, DISCARDED — doesn't reach the f→0 tail). **Q_D VERDICT: CERTIFIED no-obstruction for BOTH (3,3,3,4) AND (4,4,4,4)** — no toric ray < ½minAdm; the binding ray (coupled (x,y,r)=(1,0,1)) sits at EXACTLY ½minAdm. NOT a finiteness obstruction (construction/labour gap). **★ NOT automatic from the reduced-RLCT oracle:** Codex showed TWO oracle-compatible models (both plain-reduced-RLCT 3/2 at the anchor) — one → 7/2 (certified), one → 3/2 (OBSTRUCTION); the whole verdict hinges on `p=ν(H₁)` on the critical reduced divisor. Exact combined-ray formula: `λ(w) = (d·x + y + K)/(2·min(r, x+p, x+y+q))`, d=ab, K=ord(Jac_red)+1. cover SETTLED p (Aoyagi-independent, top level): the critical reduced divisor is the PIVOT-BLOCK-VANISHING locus with the shared deeper product Z GENERIC full-rank (e.g. (3,3,3,4) redChain (1,3,4): {A₁[0,:]=0, Z rank-3}, codim 3 = minAdm(1,3,4)); the corank rows q₁,q₂=A₁[1,:]Z, A₁[2,:]Z are generic UNITS → p=q=0 → every ray ≥½minAdm. Z-rank-deficient strata (where corank rows co-vanish, p>0) are strictly HIGHER codim = non-critical. Exact scan (toric_verify.py): p=q=0→7/2; p=0,q=1→7/2 (q HARMLESS); p=1→2 (obstruction). Both (4,4,4,4) cuts certify at 11/2. **★ TWO BUILD-CRITICAL CORRECTIONS to the #141 decorated-IH spec (relayed to formaliser):** (1) the decorated IH carries ONLY `p=ν(H₁)` + maintains the invariant `p=0 on critical reduced divisors` (geom: the corank block is TRANSVERSE to the deeper-pivot degeneration — critical divisor = pivot-vanishing, shared Z generic) — SHARPER than #141's "carry H^{−4}"; q=ν(H₂) need NOT be tracked (harmless). (2) ★ LOAD-BEARING: the correct residual decoration is `H₁^{−3}(H₁+H₂)^{−1}` (exact v-integral, → H₁^{−4} finite), NOT the `H₁^{−3}H₂^{−1}` used in the design + #141 (which