expeditions/2026-06-20-aoyagi-full/threads/14-r1-design/codex/light-recursion-answer.md:80:INFERENCE: Numeric unit coefficients need not be carried; analytic row/column unit changes preserve the ideal. But the invariant must carry at least the `diag(b)`-like symbolic data: the actual monomial exponent vector attached to each generator/row block, plus the incidence data saying which rows and hidden columns share the same variables. Equivalently, carry the weighted matrix/block support up to unit equivalence, not just total row degrees.
