expeditions/2026-06-20-aoyagi-full/threads/31-pin2-comparability/codex/fullreg-scoping-answer.md:5:**Q3.** Inference from your description: defining `deepestEFull` by reading the full `framedParams` product is the right architecture, because it matches what the loss actually sees and avoids reusing the core-zeroed object where leakage occurs. The identity `sum (deepestEFull (split w))^2 = Sreg` is provable from packing/bijection alone only if `Sreg` is already defined from the same full-product reg blocks in the same coordinates. If `Sreg` is instead defined after the `paramsSymm`/conjugation/reindexing pipeline, then the equality also needs the geometric round-trip or cert-owned identification between those full-product blocks and the loss-side blocks. General proof-theory fact: packing bijectivity proves equality between packed components and their unpacking; it does not prove that two independently produced block decompositions denote the same product. So the safe formulation is: let the cert own the full-product/block-identification geometry, and let the squeeze use only the packing identity after that identification is in hand.
